  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/elassoma-zonatum-2/",
      "html": "<p>Dwarf sunfishes are tiny fish, hardly 3 cm long, ideal for small tanks that are not heated. Elassoma zonatum is a perfect aquarium fish and as well suited as its well-known cousin Elassoma evergladei.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/elassoma-zonatum-2/",
      "html": "<p>Elassoma originate from the USA. E. zonatum originates from the eastern and central parts of the United States.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/elassoma-zonatum-2/",
      "html": "<p>Elassoma will refuse dry food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/elassoma-zonatum-2/",
      "html": "<p>Sadly the offspring is extremely small, so successful rearing can be performed by experienced hobbyists only.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/25g-perchlike-fishes-7-remaining-groups/elassoma-zonatum-2/",
      "html": "<p>Formerly only one species of the genus, Elassoma evergladei, was represented in the hobby, but in the meantime additional species have become available, among them E. zonatum. Otherwise they are easy to keep.</p>"
    }
  ],
